# Topaz v0.2.4 pretrained 2-D UDenoiseNet L2

Official Topaz pretrained weights by Tristan Bepler and colleagues, converted
without retraining to Scitomo native FORMAT 2. This is a projection-plane denoiser;
it supplies derived guidance in SC-Net workflows. It is not an SC-Net checkpoint.

Source: https://github.com/tbepler/topaz/blob/c6dde54398875dcc6a210f83de019c9165fb474c/topaz/pretrained/denoise/unet_L2_v0.2.2.sav
Revision: `c6dde54398875dcc6a210f83de019c9165fb474c`
Original SHA-256: `02709ad0bfe382f221b7ed9d4f9c14981689c2e0222e004036f925a002819c3e` (4,429,141 bytes).
Architecture: nf=48, base_width=11, top_width=5; full topology is construction.json.
All 34 source tensors are renamed without changing their values.

Inference: each V/U plane uses its own sample standard deviation (correction=1),
no outlier cutoff, and restored original intensity scaling. Projection shape,
coordinates and leading dimensions are preserved. Optional filters and vendor
tiled inference are excluded. The package is consumed by TopazProjectionDenoising.

CPU float32/float64 forward and input/parameter gradients match the pinned source
exactly for declared cases. Projection inference passes the recorded tolerances.
Evidence is under resources/; this package has no trusted CUDA/human blessing.
Constant or non-finite planes fail closed. Domain quality for any particular
tomogram requires evaluation; numerical parity does not assert denoising efficacy.

Publication: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-18952-1
Corresponding upstream source: https://github.com/tbepler/topaz/tree/c6dde54398875dcc6a210f83de019c9165fb474c
GPL-3.0 license: resources/TOPAZ_LICENSE.txt.
Native state loading requires Scitomo >=0.7.4 with safetensors.
